.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_FLAVORV_ALLOC 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_flavorv_alloc ,
.Nm ndi_flavorv_set ,
.Nm ndi_flavorv_get ,
.Nm ndi_flavor_set ,
.Nm ndi_flavor_get
.Nd associate nexus-private data with child flavors
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_flavorv_alloc
.Fa "dev_info_t *self"
.Fa "int nflavors"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_flavorv_set
.Fa "dev_info_t *self"
.Fa "ndi_flavor_t child_flavor"
.Fa "void *data"
.Fc
.Ft "void *"
.Fo ndi_flavorv_get
.Fa "dev_info_t *self"
.Fa "ndi_flavor_t child_flavor"
.Fc
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_flavor_set
.Fa "dev_info_t *child"
.Fa "ndi_flavor_t child_flavor"
.Fc
.Ft "ndi_flavor_t"
.Fo ndi_flavor_get
.Fa "dev_info_t *child"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va self
Nexus node storing pointers for its child flavors.
.It Va nflavors
Total number of supported flavors, including flavor zero.
.It Va child_flavor
Nonnegative flavor index.
.It Va data
Pointer to store for the flavor.
.It Va child
Child node whose flavor is set or retrieved.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A flavor is a small nonnegative integer identifying a kind of child supported
by a nexus.
The default flavor, \fBNDI_FLAVOR_VANILLA\fP, is zero.
\fBndi_flavor_set()\fP records a child's flavor and \fBndi_flavor_get()\fP retrieves it.
.Pp
\fBndi_flavorv_alloc()\fP reserves private-pointer slots on \fBself\fP for
\fBnflavors\fP flavors, counting flavor zero.
The count must be positive.
After allocating extra slots, a repeated allocation must specify the same
count; this function does not resize an existing vector.
Extra slots are initialized to \fBNULL\fP.
.Pp
\fBndi_flavorv_set()\fP and \fBndi_flavorv_get()\fP store and retrieve the pointer for
\fBchild_flavor\fP on the nexus.
For flavor zero they use the same pointer as \fBddi_set_driver_private()\fP and
\fBddi_get_driver_private()\fP; no extra vector is needed for that flavor.
For other flavors, the vector must have been allocated and the flavor must
be less than \fBnflavors\fP.
The functions do not validate arbitrary indices for callers.
.Pp
The framework frees the extra pointer vector after successful driver detach.
Objects referenced by the slots remain owned by the nexus driver and must be
released by it.
The flavor and pointer accessors do not lock; callers must synchronize updates
and maintain the lifetime of the nodes and pointed-to data.
.Sh CONTEXT
\fBndi_flavorv_alloc()\fP may be called from user or kernel context and
may sleep.
The other functions may also be called from interrupt context with the
necessary caller-supplied synchronization.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_flavorv_get()\fP returns the stored pointer.
\fBndi_flavor_get()\fP returns the child flavor.
The other functions have no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ddi_get_driver_private 9F ,
.Xr ndi_set_bus_private 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
